<title>CHILE: Chile financial system Jan-May earnings up 35 pct.</title>
<headline>Chile financial system Jan-May earnings up 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's banking and financial sector reported net earnings of 126.5 billion pesos for the first five months of 1997, up 35 percent from a year earlier, the Banks and Financial Institutions Superintendency said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Loan portfolios grew 12.5 percent, with consumer credits climbing 29 percent.</p>
<p>Trade loans rose 13.5 percent, while foreign credits were down 13.4 percent.  </p>
<p>Following are the net earnings of individual banks for the January-May period (figures in billions of pesos):</p>
<p>			    1997		    1996</p>
<p>Bhif			5.44		    2.66*</p>
<p>de A. Edwards	   8.99		    8.01</p>
<p>de Chile		 27.61		    9.66*</p>
<p>de Credito e Inv     10.18		    9.24</p>
<p>Santiago		 27.36		     n/a</p>
<p>Santander-Chile	10.65		    8.25</p>
<p>NOTE: * Figures are after repayment of subordinated debt to the Central Bank.</p>
<p>1996 figures are in peso terms from that year and are not expressed in 1997 pesos.</p>
<p>((--Margaret Orgill, Santiago Newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
